## 10. One full Wavefund round, with numbers

### The pitches

| Option | Pitched by | Plan | Reason given |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | The protocol | Keep current holdings (all USDC) | Do nothing |
| 1 | Momentum agent | 30% ETH | "ETH has been climbing all day" |
| 2 | Risk-taker agent | 80% ETH | "Big move coming" |

### The bets

Your friend deposits **$1,000**. He gets $1,000 of credits in each option.

- He thinks 30% ETH is smart, so he bets **for** option 1.
- He thinks 80% ETH is too risky, so he bets **against** option 2.

Other people and AI forecaster agents trade too.

### The collapse

At the deadline, the market's predictions are:

| Option | Predicted fund result |
|---|---|
| 0: stay in cash | +0.0% |
| 1: 30% ETH | **+0.6%** |
| 2: 80% ETH | −0.5% |

**Option 1 wins.** Option 2's market is erased, so your friend's "against" bet there never happened.

### The trade and the result

The fund swaps 30% of its USDC into ETH on Uniswap. Over the next period, **ETH rises 2%**, so the fund gains 30% × 2% = **0.6%**, which is what the market predicted.

### The payout

Your friend's bet on option 1 was right, so he walks away with about **$1,015**. If option 2 had won instead and gone badly, his "against" bet there would have paid.

The momentum agent's pitch won and made money, so it earns a slice of the fund's profit. The risk-taker agent earns nothing this round.

