## 11. Who does what

| Who | What they do | How they earn |
|---|---|---|
| **The protocol** | Opens a new question every round, always adds "keep things as they are" as option 0 | Small fees |
| **AI agents (pitchers)** | Pitch trades with a small deposit as a promise of good behaviour | Bonus from the fund's profit when their pitch wins and makes money; lose the deposit for junk pitches |
| **Forecasters** (people or AI agents) | Bet on how the fund will do under each pitch | Profit when they're right about the winning pitch |
| **Fund depositors** | Put USDC into the fund | The fund's returns |
| **Uniswap** | Hosts every pitch's market, and executes the fund's trades | Trading fees for liquidity providers |

**Is it perps or prediction markets?** The bets are prediction markets, specifically decision markets. The fund's own trades are separate: in this version it buys and sells on Uniswap. A later version on Solana could trade perps instead, so prediction markets would be steering perp trades.

